 "note": "PASS 65/65 at the standard gate 0.85/16 (IoU min 0.882 mean 0.902, dE mean 12.6 max 14.7). ROUND 24 (2026-09-30): the per-frame crotch row (where the legs part) was SD 51-54 vs 61-63 in the 3D for f13-f66 -- the hip block and tassets reached y 20 -> a short hip block under the fauld, small tasset lips, hip joints at y 28 and 18 px thighs (knee unchanged): IoU min 0.843 -> 0.882, dE max 16.06 -> 14.69 with the SAME poses (the documented 0.84/17.5 gate is gone). REBUILT round 20 (2026-09-30): knight.py = the standing f02 measured row by row (flat-topped helmet with keel, eye slots and finial, gorget, flat pauldrons, round breastplate with a ridge over three fauld lames, short hip block with tasset lips, legs from right under the fauld) on a two-bone IK rig: the sword fist (hx/hy/hz) drives the right arm, grip2 brings the left fist to the grip, the feet stay planted (fl/fr, crouch), the blade is aimed by sw/st; chest roll/twist about the waist (pivot_y) for the swing f20-f46 (optim fix 0 elsewhere). The gift ORB (f51-f66) is a gold lens with teardrop shape keys (drop), turn/lean/ox/oy, tan rim, speckled gold (orb_scale 14). Look: POLISHED STEEL reflecting a blotchy environment (metal 0.8, rough 0.23, env 1 at env_scale 2, world 0.37, gamma 0.95): the original armour is a mottled mirror; flat grey scored dE 14.10 vs 14.27 but lost that look. Asm frame order: unfold f02-f18 (a frame per 6), hold f17, wind-up f17-f66 (a frame per 4) -> tweens runs [[2,18],[17,66]]. No live rig (the env reflection is a world shader the live renderer cannot carry). Backups: tmp/fb_backup/knight_sprites/.",
